warning[redundant_deref]: `q.*` is not needed to reach `x`
  --> tests/lint/redundant_deref/example.jai:12:19
   |
12 |     print("%\n", q.*.x + q.y);
   |                   ^^
   |
help: write `q.x`: member access already looks through the pointer
   |
12 ~     print("%\n", q.x + q.y);
   |
   = note: `redundant_deref` is `warn` by default
